Package: longbet
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Ensemble Trees for Causal Inference on Longitudinal Data
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-09-06
Authors@R: c(
    person("Meijia", "Wang", email = "maggiew614@gmail.com", role = "aut"),
    person("P. Richard", "Hahn", role = "aut"),
    person("Ignacio", "Martinez", email = "martinezig@google.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: Time-varying heterogeneous treatment effects in panel data with
  Bayesian causal forests. LongBet models the prognostic and treatment surfaces
  with separate forests, gives exposure dynamics a shared Gaussian-process
  trajectory, and absorbs unobserved unit heterogeneity with unit random
  intercepts. Fitting is done by a vectorized Metropolis-Hastings sampler
  written in JAX and shipped as the 'longbet-jax' Python package, which this
  package drives through 'reticulate'; it runs on CPU or GPU and reports
  multi-chain convergence diagnostics.
License: Apache License (== 2.0)
URL: https://github.com/ignacio82/longbet-jax
BugReports: https://github.com/ignacio82/longbet-jax/issues
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.10) with the longbet-jax package
